policy errors.rules: DeployApproval [1:1-39:21]
  use deploy.common.{cleared} [6:1-6:28]
  param min_soak: duration = 24h [3:1-3:31]
  when cleared { [9:1-12:2]
    pub let tmp = release.soak [10:3-10:29]
    deny(tmp) [11:3-11:12]
  }
  when <error> { [15:1-17:2]
    deny(chain) [16:3-16:14]
  }
  when <error> { [20:1-22:2]
    deny(paren) [21:3-21:14]
  }
  when cleared { [28:1-30:2]
  }
  when cleared { [33:1-35:2]
    approve(fine, bake: 15m) [34:3-34:27]
  }
  let tight = min_soak [39:1-39:21]

== diagnostics ==

errors_policy.sigil:6:1: `use` must come before every other statement
  |
6 | use deploy.common.{cleared}
  | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  = help: move it up, right after the header

errors_policy.sigil:10:3: a let inside a `when` body can't be `pub`
   |
10 |   pub let tmp = release.soak
   |   ^^^
   = help: only top-level lets can be exported; remove `pub`

errors_policy.sigil:15:30: `<` can't follow `<`: comparisons don't chain
   |
15 | when release.soak < min_soak < 2h {
   |                              ^
   = help: add parentheses to say which comparison happens first, or join two comparisons with `and`

errors_policy.sigil:20:33: expected `)`, found `{`
   |
20 | when (release.hotfix or cleared {
   |                                 ^
   = help: to close the `(` at 20:6

errors_policy.sigil:25:1: expected a statement, found `guardrails`
   |
25 | guardrails
   | ^^^^^^^^^^
   = help: a bare name isn't a statement; an invocation needs parentheses, like `guardrails()`

errors_policy.sigil:29:17: expected a named argument, found `"extra"`
   |
29 |   review(owner, "extra", approvers: approvers)
   |                 ^^^^^^^
   = help: after the reason, every argument is written `name: value`, like `approvers: ["payments-leads"]`

errors_policy.sigil:39:21: `---` separates documents and can't appear inside an expression
   |
39 | let tight = min_soak---1h
   |                     ^^^
   = help: if you meant arithmetic, put spaces between the minus signs
